                <pb facs="0433" n="309" sameAs="frus:frus1923v02/pg309"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">125.655/89: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Wheeler</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-06-07T15:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 7, 1923—3
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 4:34 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>211. The city council of Newcastle-on-Tyne last night adopted a resolution urging
                    the Government to come to a settlement with the United States that would secure
                    the reopening of the American consulate there.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wheeler</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
